###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The GDML model is stated to be three orders of magnitude faster than DFT;
# no absolute timing or hardware is given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Per-molecule force and energy errors are in supplementary tables S1 and S3, not in the PDF read; the main text gives only the target force accuracy of 1 kcal/mol/A reached with about 1000 samples and an energy error of about 0.2 kcal/mol. No AccuracyMetric is encoded.
# - Kernel, descriptor and regularisation hyperparameters are not stated in the main text.
# - Classical and path-integral MD of aspirin at 300 K with the GDML model are demonstrated (interatomic distance and dihedral distributions); these are figures.
# - The manifest classes this paper as 'Application/model instance'; it is the originating GDML method paper (registry origin of entity:GDML).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
